# XCU nohup
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The behaviour when standard output or standard error is a terminal
# cannot be tested without one, so the tests run with all three streams
# on files or pipes. That is the situation of a test run by the driver.

assertion  XCU.nohup.001
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#ASYNCHRONOUS EVENTS
class      required
since      1992
says       The utility run by nohup has SIGHUP ignored: a shell started by
           nohup that sends SIGHUP to itself carries on.
note       The test first checks that a shell not started by nohup is
           ended by the same signal. If the test shell already ignores
           SIGHUP the result is UNRESOLVED.
test       t/001-hup-ignored.sh

assertion  XCU.nohup.002
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       When standard output is not a terminal, nohup writes the
           utility's output to standard output with the arguments passed
           on, and creates no nohup.out in the current directory or in
           HOME.
test       t/002-stdout-passthrough.sh

assertion  XCU.nohup.003
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#EXIT STATUS
class      required
since      1992
says       nohup exits with the status of the utility, 127 when the utility
           cannot be found, and 126 when it is found but cannot be run.
test       t/003-status.sh

assertion  XCU.nohup.004
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/nohup.html#STDERR
class      required
since      1992
says       When standard error is not a terminal the utility's standard
           error is not redirected: what it writes there reaches standard
           error and nohup writes nothing of its own to it.
test       t/004-stderr-passthrough.sh
